<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The asset post-processing pipeline (M8-06): `15` §B4's seven steps, the Part F QA checklist and
    the §A4 silhouette gate, as a library with a thin CLI over it.

    It sits under tools/ beside AssetManifest, BalanceHarness, ContentValidator and EconomySim
    because it ships to nobody. Nothing in src/ references it and no game rule calls it — it is a
    production-pipeline tool that turns a generated image into a delivery-format one. It is an Exe
    for the same reason the other three are: a human runs it over a batch. The types stay public so
    the test suite and M8-10 (which enumerates the manifest, generates one placeholder per uncut
    slot and drives the whole pipeline) can call it as a library.

    🔒 SkiaSharp, NOT SixLabors.ImageSharp. ImageSharp moved to the Six Labors Split License at
    v3.0, which requires a paid commercial licence above a revenue threshold — the same lock-in
    that cost this repository its previous assertion library (M1-00). SkiaSharp is MIT.
    SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux is not optional: CI runs on ubuntu-24.04 and every Skia call
    throws DllNotFoundException without it.

    🔒 No native binaries. There is no shelling out to ImageMagick, pngquant, oxipng or cwebp
    anywhere in this project — managed code only, so the toolchain stays hermetic and CI-portable.
    Where that costs `15` §B4 a capability (Lanczos in step 5, pngquant in step 6) the step emits a
    DeclaredDeviation rather than pretending.

    🔒 It does NOT read game-data/assets/*.json itself. M8-09 already wrote that reader, so this
    project ProjectReferences SlayIdleRepeat.AssetManifest and takes ArtAsset/AssetManifestSet as
    input. A second manifest parser would be a second place for `15`'s holes to be silently
    defaulted; SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPipeline.Tests pins that there is only one.

    🔒 Central Package Management is live (Directory.Packages.props), so a Version= attribute on a
    PackageReference here is an error (NU1008). The two SkiaSharp rows are deliberately absent from
    build/ci/non-vendor-packages.json: leaving them off the allow-list is what keeps a
    native-binary dependency contained to exactly this project.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPipeline</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SlayIdleRepeat.AssetPipeline</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" />
    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\AssetManifest\SlayIdleRepeat.AssetManifest.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
